From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] notifications: ask the calendar in the one place that has an
 answer to give

Patch 0042 skipped creating the calendar trackers when no calendar provider is
installed. evaluateSubscriptionsW() then had no tracker to ask, kept the
CheckEventResult it starts at null, and read a field of it: system_server threw
NullPointerException at EventConditionProvider.java:256 every time the event
rule was evaluated, which on PW3 Android Test V50 restarted the framework every
14 seconds and never reached the launcher.

The check moves into CalendarTracker.checkEvent(), which still has to return an
answer and now returns one: no event, recheck a day later. The trackers exist as
they do on any device, nothing queries a provider that is not installed, and the
error lines 0042 set out to remove stay away.

